# Bellbound Monk visual review

## Identity and camera

Original CT02 is a stout ochre-robed cultist with charcoal cowl/cuffs, blank oval brass mask, two dark gloves stacked on a single bell handle and chunky shoes. All14 animation drawings keep this count and silhouette identity. Hood/shoulder upper planes are more prominent than in the static portrait. Heading stays three-quarter screen-down-right. Exact camera values remain an unverified painted approximation.

## Locomotion by drawing

1. Low compress, bell tilted right. Two hands share the handle; one intact flared bell and clapper.
2. Body lifts and robe tail sweeps left; bell lags left. No ordinary alternating walk step is imposed.
3. Clear buoyant high point with shoes tucked and robe expanded. Bell swings right without extra handle.
4. Broad trailing robe and far-right bell read as inertial overshoot. Complete bell lip retained beyond original nominalcell.
5. Compressed low robe silhouette, bell more centered and downward. Both grips stay attached.
6. Rebound with large robe mass and rightward bell. Wrap to1 is readable but retains a small stepped compression/pop, appropriate to an animation test rather than polished final.

Ordered transitions inspected:1→2 lift,2→3 apex,3→4 broad drag,4→5 squash,5→6 rebound,6→1 next compress. Large cloth/body shape changes are expressive, with minor generated-volume inconsistency disclosed.

## Toll by drawing

1. Weighted ready, original identity clear.
2. Two hands draw bell toward chest; elbows fold.
3. Loaded back-coil with the bell raised to mask level. Mask stays blank and glove/handle count stays intact.
4. Torso and bell drive down-right; single small elliptical wave starts below the one bell mouth.
5. Deep overshoot and broad ground-plane ring. Goldring breaks are intentional; complete disconnected arcs retained.
6. Body recoils upward; two broad wave fragments fade around the lower body. No fragment was deleted as speckle.
7. Heavy return, robe swing and lowering bell.
8. Quiet weighted ready return with clean bell grip.

Ordered transitions inspected:1→2→3 anticipation;3→4 sharp release;4→5 weight/impact;5→6 recoil with outward wave progression;6→7→8 slow settle. Cast8→1 is a review repeat only; runtime cast is non-looping.

